# Undo against the computer takes back the player's last turn and the computer's reply (Easy, playing White).
# Layout (1400x800): Undo (558,90), Submit (841,90); Versus (150,250), Computer (833,122), Easy (644,226), Standard (690,320), Play (808,712).
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 833 122        # Computer
wait 20
click 644 226        # Easy
wait 10
click 690 320        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
capture vs-undo-nothing-yet          # Undo is disabled: nothing has been played
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 40
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 40
click 841 90         # Submit
waitai
wait 90
capture vs-undo-before               # turns 1 and 1b played
clicksq 0 2 d2
wait 40
clicksq 0 2 d4
wait 40
click 558 90         # Undo: only the unsubmitted move goes
wait 40
capture vs-undo-pending-move         # d4 is back on d2; the first turn pair is still there
click 558 90         # Undo again: the turn and the computer's reply
wait 60
capture vs-undo-after                # the starting position, White to move, Turn 1
clicksq 0 0 d2
wait 40
clicksq 0 0 d4
wait 40
ainodes 0
click 841 90         # a different move ...
wait 20
click 558 90         # ... taken back while the computer is still thinking: its search is cancelled
wait 60
capture vs-undo-while-thinking       # the starting position again, nothing is thinking
ainodes 400
wait 60
capture vs-undo-search-cancelled     # still the player's turn after the search could have finished
